(a) The position of clerk of the municipal court is created. The clerk shall be appointed by the city manager. The clerk shall work under the general supervision of the chief of police, with the consent of the city manager. The chief of police shall evaluate the performance of the clerk of court, shall consult with the solicitor and judge on their evaluation of the clerk of the court's performance, and report the results of the evaluation once annually to the city manager. The clerk of court shall supervise the functional day-to-day office activities of all classified municipal court employees. It is recognized that the municipal judge and solicitor shall direct the activities of the employees respectively assigned to them for specific work assignments and procedures; however, the clerk of court shall have supervisory responsibility over all classified employees assigned to the municipal court office to assure that the municipal court budget and provisions of the City Code and Charter as they apply to employee performance and employee conduct will be effectively and consistently administrated.
(b) The clerk of court shall:
(1) Prepare all subpoenas and warrants and maintain a docket thereof that will show the name of the person for whom the subpoena or warrant was issued, its date, at whose instance it was issued, and to whom delivered; the municipal judge may require that the clerk maintain a duplicate court docket and to use the signed duplicate copy of the docket to make necessary entries in the master docket after each session of court;
(2) Be authorized to make continuations of a case for good cause shown;
(3) Act as court officer to accept filing of all pleadings and motions;
(4) Indicate time and date of receipt;
(5) Schedule hearings upon motions when necessary and notify parties and witnesses;
(6) Open files with copy of original citations for solicitor in cases where motions are filed and act as custodian of these files;
(7) Act as custodian of the seal of the court; custodian of the original citation issued by the police department; and custodian of the master docket of the court;
(8) Certify copies of citations, orders and sentences where necessary;
(9) Handle correspondence with the department of public safety regarding cancellation, revocation and suspension of licenses, and forward all convictions, bond forfeitures and other disposition reports required by O.C.G.A. § 40-5-53;
(10) Forward to the department of public safety all licenses received by the court pursuant to O.C.G.A. § 40-5-53;
(11) Perform other related duties as assigned.
(Ord. of 11-18-2013, § 34-4)

